----- stdout -----
Check readiness to activate without making any changes (alias: doctor)

Usage: nails check [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -c, --config <PATH>
          Path to the configuration file (overrides binary-relative discovery)

      --overlay-only
          Check as for an overlay-only activation (skip the NixOS profile checks)

      --flake <FLAKE_REF>
          Check against a specific NixOS flake reference (e.g. /etc/nixos#hostname)

  -v, --verbose...
          More diagnostics on stderr: -v for debug, -vv for trace

      --allow-persistent-journal
          Report a persistent decoy journal as a warning instead of a failure

          Mirrors `activate --allow-persistent-journal` so `check`/`--dry-run` reflects what activation would do.

  -q, --quiet
          Print only errors and the final result

      --color <WHEN>
          When to use colour

          Possible values:
          - auto:   Colour a stream only when it is a terminal, TERM is not `dumb` and NO_COLOR is unset or empty
          - always: Always colour, even when piped
          - never:  Never colour

          [default: auto]

      --ascii
          Use ASCII markers instead of Unicode symbols and box drawing

      --json
          Print machine-readable JSON on stdout

      --no-log-file
          Do not write the log file on the hidden volume (diagnostics still go to stderr)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

----- stderr -----
